---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 6, 2025";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Nimio"
  description="Nimio's privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data."
  ogImage="/og/nimio-og.svg"
>
  <main class="px-6 py-16">
    <article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl">

      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-nimio-coral">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-nimio-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-nimio-ink/60">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose-nimio mt-10 space-y-10 text-nimio-ink/80 leading-relaxed">

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">1. Overview</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Nimio ("we", "us", or "our") is an open-source, privacy-first platform for intentional availability.
            This policy explains what personal data we collect when you use the Nimio Android app and website
            (<a href="https://nimio.org" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">nimio.org</a>),
            why we collect it, and how it is protected.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with advertisers or third-party data brokers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">2. Data We Collect</h2>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Account information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            When you create an account we collect your <strong>email address</strong> and a securely hashed
            password (we never store your plaintext password). If you sign in with Google, we receive a
            Google account identifier and your email address from Google's OAuth service — we do not receive
            your Google password.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Profile information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You may optionally provide a <strong>username</strong>, <strong>display name</strong>,
            <strong>avatar image</strong>, and a short <strong>bio</strong>. This information is visible
            to other Nimio users you connect with according to your privacy settings.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Availability status</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            The core function of Nimio is sharing your intentional availability state (e.g. Free, Busy,
            Want to talk) with people you choose. Status data is stored on our servers and shared only
            with the connections you explicitly approve and at the visibility tier you configure.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Connection data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We store records of the connections and relationship tiers you establish with other users so
            that your privacy preferences can be enforced correctly.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Technical and session data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We store <strong>refresh tokens</strong> (as a secure hash) to keep you signed in. Standard
            server logs may record IP addresses and request metadata for security and debugging purposes.
            These logs are retained for a limited period and are not used for profiling or advertising.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-nimio-ink">Data we do NOT collect</h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
            <li>Device location</li>
            <li>Contacts or address book</li>
            <li>Camera or microphone access</li>
            <li>Any advertising identifier (GAID or similar)</li>
            <li>Precise behavioural analytics or tracking pixels</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">The app requires only the <code class="rounded bg-nimio-sand px-1 text-sm">INTERNET</code> permission to communicate with our API.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>To create and maintain your account and authenticate you securely.</li>
            <li>To deliver the core availability-sharing features of Nimio.</li>
            <li>To send a one-time email verification link when you register.</li>
            <li>To detect and prevent abuse, fraud, and security incidents.</li>
            <li>To improve the reliability and performance of the service.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">We do not use your data for advertising, profiling, or sale to third parties.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">4. Data Sharing</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not sell or rent your personal data. We may share data only in the following limited circumstances:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Infrastructure providers</strong> — cloud hosting and database services necessary to run
              Nimio. These providers process data only on our behalf and under contractual confidentiality obligations.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Sign-In</strong> — if you choose to sign in with Google, authentication is handled
              by Google's OAuth 2.0 service, subject to
              <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal obligations</strong> — if required by law, court order, or to protect the rights and
              safety of users or the public.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">5. Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your account data is retained for as long as your account is active. You may request deletion
            of your account at any time (see Section 7). When an account is deleted we remove your personal
            data from our active systems. Anonymised or aggregated data that cannot be linked back to you
            may be retained for service improvement purposes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">6. Security</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use industry-standard practices to protect your data: passwords are stored as
            cryptographic hashes (bcrypt), all traffic between the app and our API is encrypted with
            TLS, and authentication tokens are stored as secure hashes. We review our security practices
            regularly. No method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, but we take
            reasonable measures to protect your information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">7. Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">You have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
            <li><strong>Delete</strong> your account and associated personal data.</li>
            <li><strong>Export</strong> a copy of your data.</li>
            <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> for optional data processing at any time.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:privacy@nimio.org" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">privacy@nimio.org</a>.
            We will respond within 30 days.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            For account deletion request steps and retention details, see
            <a href="/delete-account" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">Delete Your Account</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Nimio is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
            data from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data,
            please contact us and we will delete it promptly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last updated"
            date at the top of this page. For significant changes we will notify users via the app or
            email. Continued use of Nimio after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nimio-ink">10. Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you have questions or concerns about this privacy policy or our data practices, please
            reach out:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
            <li>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@nimio.org" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">privacy@nimio.org</a></li>
            <li>GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/nimio-app" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline decoration-nimio-coral/50 hover:text-nimio-coral">github.com/nimio-app</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="focus-ring rounded-full bg-nimio-ocean px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-[#e51d5c]"
        >
          Back to Nimio
        </a>
      </div>

    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
